So far, Pretty Little Liars Season 6 has been a lot more about the Liars and their road to recovery and a lot less about Charles.
And while the change of focus has been refreshing, the nagging about Charles' motives still lingers in the back of our minds unforgettably.
More: PLL Season 6 premiere: The Liars aren't who they used to be
Sasha Pieterse, who plays Alison DiLaurentis, confirmed that Charles is somehow related to the DiLaurentis family when we interviewed her before the start of Season 6. But that can't be his only connection to Rosewood. Otherwise, why torment Aria (Lucy Hale), Spencer (Troian Bellisario), Hanna (Ashley Benson) and Emily (Shay Mitchell) as well?
If he's related to Alison, then he also has a connection to Spencer. Spencer and Jason are half-siblings since Spencer's dad had an affair with Jason's mom back in the day.
But that doesn't explain why he's after Aria and Hanna.
My theory is that it all comes back to the night Alison went missing. Charles could have been a patient at Radley and that could have been the night he escaped, meaning he was there when everything went down and was, ultimately, somehow responsible for the catalyst that caused that series of events.
My guess is he went after Sara Harvey on accident, thinking she was Alison. So instead of getting Alison that night, he ended up with Sara in his dollhouse and made do with her as his Alison until he got his hands on Mona.
I think he wants to recreate the life he never had, with family and friends surrounding him, instead of the clear solitude he exists in now.
More: PLL's I. Marlene King reveals bombshell A spoiler (VIDEO)
But why the DiLaurentises are in the dark about his existence is one of the key mysteries on the show.
