Gamers around the world are becoming familiar with the name of a city-sanctioned Portland homeless community.
Grand Theft Auto V, released Sept. 17, features a homeless camp called Dignity Village -- the name that a non-profit "transitional campground" in Northeast Portland claimed more than a decade ago.
Nancy Mottaz, who identified herself as the camp's CEO, said the non-profit is looking into the situation with an attorney, but declined to comment further.
Rockstar Games, the publisher of Grand Theft Auto V, has not returned requests for comment. The story was first reported by Street Roots, a Portland newspaper focusing on homeless issues.
A YouTube video that a player made shows a homeless camp at the edge of a city, near a freeway that runs along a coastline. Portland's Dignity Village is a half-mile south of Northeast Marine Drive, which runs parallel to the Columbia River.
